      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nashoba%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nashoba comes from the Choctaw word for wolf, and the area was often referred to as Wolf County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nashoba%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A United States Post Office first opened at Nashoba, Indian Territory, on September 13, 1886.",
